5. IMPORTANT EXAM QUESTIONS & ANSWERS:
Q 1: Differentiate between Method Overloading and Method Overriding.
Answer: Overloading occurs in the same class with different parameters (compile-time polymorphism). Overriding occurs between
superclass and subclass with identical signatures (runtime polymorphism). Return type alone is insufficient for overloading.
Q 2: Compare Abstract Classes and Interfaces in Java.
Answer: Abstract classes can have instance variables and concrete methods, supporting single inheritance. Interfaces cannot hold
instance state (only public static final constants) and allow multiple inheritance of type.

